    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe one endpoint affected is `POST /api/owners`. I added an idempotency gate at the front of its OfficeFloor pipeline and a recording step at the back, following the project's function-injection conventions (one small class per step, wired in YAML).\n\n**New pieces:**\n\n- **`IdempotencyStore`** (`@Component`) \u2014 an application-scoped, thread-safe (`ConcurrentHashMap`) map from `Idempotency-Key` \u2192 created owner id. `record(...)` uses `putIfAbsent` so the first create wins.\n\n- **`CheckIdempotency`** \u2014 the new entry step. Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and routes to exactly one of two outputs: `existing` (a key already seen \u2192 replay) or `proceed` (new/absent key \u2192 normal create).\n\n- **`RespondWithExistingOwner`** \u2014 the `existing` branch target: loads the owner the key first created and responds **200** (versus `RespondWithOwnerCreated`'s 201).\n\n- **`RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 runs after `SaveOwner`, registering the key against the generated owner id.\n\n**YAML** (`owners.POST.yml`): `checkIdempotency` is now the first step with `outputs: { existing, proceed }`, and `recordIdempotency` was spliced in between `save` and `audit` inside the existing transaction governance.\n\n## Two things worth noting\n\n1. **Branching mechanism.** My first attempt used a single `@Flow` plus a `next:` fall-through, but this OfficeFloor version ran *both* the invoked flow and `next` (creating the duplicate \u2192 409). I switched to two explicit flow outputs (`existing`/`proceed`) with no `next:`, so exactly one branch runs.\n\n2. **Header binding.** Spring's `@RequestHeader` silently resolved to `null` here (the starter lists it as a supported arg type, but it didn't actually read the header \u2014 only `@PathVariable`/`@RequestParam`/`@RequestBody` are called out in AGENTS.md). I used OfficeFloor's native `@HttpHeaderParameter(\"Idempotency-Key\")`, which resolves correctly and returns `null` when the header is absent, so ordinary keyless creates are unaffected.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` passes (repeat with same key \u2192 200, same id), and the full suite is green (10/10). I removed the temporary debug logging I'd added during diagnosis.",
